{%- comment -%}
  Outputs "true" when the product should show its options as the near-title
  combined-listing selector (combined-listing-selector.liquid), otherwise "false".

  Liquid has no property that reports whether a product is a combined listing
  parent or child, so this branches on product_option_value.product_url, which
  Shopify documents as the signal for combined-listing navigation: it is only
  populated for option values that belong to a sibling product. The selector
  applies to single-option families (e.g. Turf Grade) where at least one value
  points to a different product than the one being viewed. Multi-option
  families (the hex dumbbell parents) keep the standard variant picker.

  Usage:
    {%- capture applies -%}{%- render 'combined-listing-selector-applies', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}

  Accepts:
    product - {Object} the product to check (required)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign applies = false
  if product.options_with_values.size == 1
    assign cl_option = product.options_with_values.first
    if cl_option.values.size > 1
      assign current_url = product.url | split: '?' | first
      for value in cl_option.values
        if value.product_url != blank
          assign value_base_url = value.product_url | split: '?' | first
          if value_base_url != current_url
            assign applies = true
            break
          endif
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  endif
  echo applies
-%}
